/*! \page sdk_class_a_cuda Class-A CUDA Authoring

Markdown companion: \c docs/class_a_cuda_authoring.md (normative depth).

\section sdk_a_depths Replacement depths

| Kind | Interface | Output |
|------|-----------|--------|
| CE | \c 0x00010003 | Full-slot CF32 H + F32 noise |
| Equalizer | \c 0x00010004 | Compact CF32 symbols + post-EQ noise |
| Receiver | \c 0x00010005 | Compact FP16 LLRs pre-descramble |

\section sdk_a_rules Hot-path rules

- Pure \c ocudu_dapp_query_v1 (no CUDA init in query).
- Enqueue only on \c invocation.execution_stream; do not host-synchronize.
- Allocate weights and scratch in prepare / model / worker create.
- Per-lane worker state for concurrent PUSCH.
- \c noexcept ABI callbacks with \c guard_algorithm_call for algorithm code.
- Profile in descriptor must match hash-bound manifest.
- v1 envelope: two layers max, all QAM, DM-RS 1/2, no transform precoding.

\section sdk_a_metrics Host metrics

\c class_a.fallback.* counts host bypass reasons.
\c class_a.completion.deadline_misses counts late GPU completion without
rewinding the current result through conventional fallback.

\section sdk_a_cert Certify before catalog

\code{.sh}
certify_class_a_cuda my_module.so 0x00010005
\endcode

\section sdk_a_run Enable on a DU

Stage \c .so + manifest + SBOM, list under \c package_manifests, then E3
\c load (in-process / cuda|cpu) → prepare → arm → shadow → activate.
Copy-paste for every Class-A reference: Markdown \c docs/run_examples.md §1–§2
and the enable section of \c docs/class_a_cuda_authoring.md.

*/
